framework ArchitectureDecisionRecord:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain ADR0028:
  description "ADR-0028 revision 2: Versioned conscious agency contract. Status Accepted; no supersession."

problem P1:
  |
    Accepted requirement revision 1 needs executable boundaries for goal legitimacy,
    reaction projection, state ownership, partial acceptance and immutable activation.
    A goal field alone cannot fix the current missing goal-to-conscious-input path.

premise AUTHORITY:
  |
    Owner correction on 2026-09-09: author confirmation is irrelevant; goal
    legitimacy depends on character personality and known counterpart relationships.
    Requirement v1 remains an exact historical accepted snapshot, but its R1
    author-explicit precedence is no longer the current goal criterion.
    docs/character-agency-requirements-v2.md records the corrected candidate at step1,
    not inherited acceptance. ADR0027 retains psyche/conscious/engine ownership;
    ADR0025/0026 retain old V2 contracts, ADR0011 structured assets and action norms,
    ADR0018 activation. This revision supersedes no Accepted ADR.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Revision1 chose author-confirmed provenance and unknown-origin blocking.
    That choice answered the wrong question and is withdrawn.
    Revision2 proposes goal derivation within the existing conscious call from
    personality, values, known relationships and current context, independent of
    who authored or confirmed a suggested objective. No origin attestation or
    extra critic is required. Victory remains the ordinary compatible fallback.

evidence E_OWNER_CORRECTION:
  |
    Owner stated: 作者が確認した目標かどうかは問題ない。
    単に、キャラ性格と相手などの関係性から、正当な目標かどうかがポイントです。
    The subsequent semantic criterion is a correction, not revision1's original intent.

evidence E_REVIEW:
  |
    Independent review report docs/evidence/character-agency-requirements-v1-independent-review-2026-09-09.md
    reviewed only requirement v1, not this correction. Its provenance suggestion is
    historical, not a current requirement. Other remaining gaps are
    bounded reaction projection, detailed generation/accounting and untested quality.

evidence E_CODE:
  |
    free-action-service.ts decisionProfileForSheet injects victory when profile is absent.
    openai-compatible.ts authoring prompts also permit generated victory profiles.
    DecisionProfileSchema lacks origin metadata. That absence does not require
    author confirmation, a new envelope or blocked battle creation.
    psyche-reaction-policy.ts returns actionProjection and expressionProjection.
    dialogue-pipeline-settings.ts currently writes schemaVersion 2. provider retry
    permits at most two total retries; the accounting taxonomy includes both
    advanceCharacterAgentCompact and decideCharacterAction under characterExpression.

evidence E_BASELINE:
  |
    CA-00 docs/evidence/character-agency-ca00-inventory-2026-09-09.md verifies the
    actual adapter boundary, SQLite goal retention and CAS, but goal absence in
    conscious input; later perception carries the already-spoken line. This is
    synthetic baseline evidence, not proof of Grok improvement or V3 implementation.

decision D1 based_on P1, AUTHORITY, OPTIONS, E_CODE, E_OWNER_CORRECTION:
  |
    A legitimate upper goal is justified by the bound character personality, values,
    known counterpart relationship and situation. The same conscious call derives it.
    Authorship and owner confirmation do not make a goal legitimate or illegitimate.
    Existing defaultObjective text, if present in the bound definition, is suggested
    goal context, not a privileged constraint. Even an explicitly supplied objective
    must be assessed for fit; generated goals are not rejected merely for being generated.
    Where no more fitting goal follows, winning is the ordinary fallback, not a
    value that overrides enjoying combat or protecting a known counterpart.
    Existing action prohibitions remain engine constraints; distinguish them from
    descriptive objective text. Do not infer unknown counterpart attributes.
    Reuse existing character envelope and definition revisions and bind their
    snapshots/digests in the V3 battle contract. Remove agencyObjectiveV1,
    objectiveAuthority, CharacterGenerationEnvelopeV3 and owner reconfirmation.
    No AGENCY_OBJECTIVE_PROVENANCE_REQUIRED error or origin-based start rejection.
    Absent origin metadata is not missing personality data and is not a failure.
    Prompt and fixtures judge semantic fit with allowed goal/action sets, not exact
    wording, source identity, victory alone or proof of author approval.
    Existing goal basisRefs link the relevant context. Schema/ref validity alone
    does not prove semantic fit; no deterministic semantic oracle or extra critic
    call is introduced. Actual model quality remains to be evaluated.

decision D2 based_on D1, AUTHORITY, E_CODE:
  |
    New BattleAssetManifest schemaVersion 3 binds dialogue schemaVersion 3 with
    contextProjectionMode compact, character generation digests and compilerInputsV3,
    plus psyche-reaction-policy-v1. Keep manifest/dialogue V1/V2 decoders unchanged.
    Runtime selects on the complete frozen discriminator tuple; missing or mixed
    V3 bindings fail BATTLE_CONTRACT_MISMATCH, never route to legacy implicitly.
    No current setting or mutable character is reread during battle execution.
    Extend existing settings update request with optional schemaVersion 2|3.
    Omitted version preserves persisted 3, otherwise keeps the existing write-2
    behavior. Explicit 3 requires compact. Explicit 2 allows the existing modes.
    Preserve expectedRevision CAS and same-transaction settings generation creation.
    Incompatible legacy mode against V3 is rejected, not silently downgraded.
    Default settings remain unchanged. V3 plus a legacy deployment override fails
    before battle creation; no environment switch may upgrade an existing tuple.
    ADR0018 persisted-setting authority and isolated override identity stay in force.
    Selecting V3 globally or deploying remains separately
    authorized; authoring this ADR does not execute any of those changes.

decision D3 based_on D2, AUTHORITY, E_CODE:
  |
    V3 private reaction state uses existing bounded ReactionStateV1 and fixed traits.
    Prologue initializes initialPsycheReactionStateV1 without inventing an observation.
    Turn and aftermath apply the existing deterministic policy once at their existing
    phase commit boundary to validated normalized experience. Missing features never
    escalate to an LLM. Missing input keeps the last valid state; real empty input may
    decay normally. Projection must not invoke another transition or decay.
    Extract a pure projection helper preserving the existing V1 projection formula.
    Each V3 conscious input, including later redecision, receives reaction:
    {action:PsycheReactionProjectionV1, expression:PsycheReactionProjectionV1}.
    Fields are schemaVersion 1, arousal low|medium|high, interpretation max3 of
    adverse|uncertain|affiliative, impulse max4 of
    confront|withdraw|approach|seek_reassurance. Expression additionally requires
    expressionTendency withhold|restrained|available. These are tendencies, not
    forced action or forced silence. No raw traits, scores or transition evidence
    enter conscious input. Server-only transition evidence keeps its existing owner.
    Later redecision reads the last reaction projection without another reaction tick.
    Psyche receives no ability metadata, plan, utterance proposal or engine knowledge.
    Future special-moment LLM and direct conscious regulation remain unspecified.

decision D4 based_on D1, D2, D3, AUTHORITY:
  |
    CharacterAgentState.consciousAgencyV1 is closed:
    {schemaVersion:1, upperGoal:Goal|null, latestDecision:Decision|null}.
    Goal={statement:nonblank 1..240, basisRefs:unique nonempty refs 1..6}.
    Intent={aim:nonblank 1..160, basisRefs:unique nonempty refs 1..8,
    rationale:nonblank 1..240}.
    Decision={intent:Intent, action:existing validated Action|null,
    turn:server integer >=0, phase:prologue|turn|later}.
    All strings use trim then Zod UTF-16 string length; refs max96.
    Initialize both nullable fields to null only for a new V3 battle.
    Conscious output is the sole goal/intent proposer; the acceptance function is
    the sole writer, persisted only under the existing battle revision CAS.
    Upper goal is set once, then immutable for this slice. Latest decision is the
    latest accepted proposal, not executed result; no new event/operation ID or ledger.
    Subsequent judgment receives it explicitly as previous accepted proposal.
    Engine fallbacks never reuse it as their own intent. Existing rejection/phase
    evidence, current perception and current candidate list distinguish actual results.
    No narration/opponent/provider convenience state may write this object.

decision D5 based_on D3, D4, AUTHORITY, E_BASELINE:
  |
    V3 normal input is closed and includes contractVersion:3, phase, character
    self-profile, structuredSelf, reaction, agencyState, goalPolicy, facts,
    turnObservation, utteranceHistory, observableManifestations, social and
    counterpart when permitted, and decision in prologue/turn only.
    Keep self-reference and voice from the bound conscious-self profile, not old
    private psyche prose. goalPolicy states semantic-fit derivation from personality,
    values, known relationship and context, with ordinary compatible victory fallback.
    Existing objective text is non-privileged context; owner-confirmation flags are absent. structuredSelf includes known relationship only.
    Facts are max128 closed {ref, kind, sourcePath} entries. kind is
    suggested_objective|value|relationship|default_objective|ability|reserve|observation|candidate.
    sourcePath is a server-constructed JSON pointer into an allowlisted part of this
    frozen input, never an arbitrary model path or private server object. ref is
    unique, <=96 chars, deterministically assigned within this input. Immutable
    goal-source refs remain stable across calls of the bound battle; current fact
    refs are valid only for that input. Do not truncate mandatory rules to fit a
    bound; overflow fails input construction before dispatch with a recorded error.
    Goal basis refs accept only first four kinds. Intent refs may use all kinds.
    Acceptance checks membership/kind, not inferred semantic truth. No hidden
    counterpart fact, numeric hidden trait or narrator text is added via this table.
    Previously accepted goal/intent refs are historical context, not current facts;
    do not revalidate old refs against a new observation set or treat them as fresh.
    Utterance history contains only already-committed, observer-permitted occurrences.
    Keep existing history window; identical text is legal. Never use lastSpeech
    as new semantic input or persist a new lastSpeech write.
    Later input includes contractVersion:3, phase:later, character, structuredSelf,
    reaction, agencyState, goalPolicy, facts, current perception, decision and
    committed self utterances in the current phase. It shares goal and intent
    with normal consciousness but neither re-speaks nor declares execution.
    No new manifestation generator is introduced: only eligible existing validated
    observer-safe proposals may be offered, otherwise the list is empty. Realization
    is exact membership in that list; private causes or new bodily effects are illegal.

decision D6 based_on D4, D5, AUTHORITY:
  |
    Closed prologue/turn response requires exactly initialGoal, intent, nextAction,
    nextUtterance, realizedManifestation. initialGoal is Goal when uninitialized and
    null when initialized. intent is Intent; nextAction is existing action proposal
    or null; nextUtterance and realizedManifestation retain existing value domains
    and utterance coercion/validation, with null speech legal as in the requirement.
    Closed aftermath response has only nextUtterance and realizedManifestation.
    Closed later response has only intent and nextAction; it cannot write the goal.
    No unrestricted record/unknown final contract, unjustified casts or internal
    stringify/reparse. Untrusted JSON is parsed once at the network boundary,
    then safe-decoded field by field into a typed acceptance result.
    Envelope object shape, extra keys and phase-forbidden keys are checked
    first; an invalid envelope rejects all proposals. Missing required fields are
    per-field failures so independent valid speech may still be accepted.
    An initialized goal with a non-null replacement is a goal-field failure; keep
    old goal and reject dependent intent/action for that response.
    Precedence after a valid envelope:
    - invalid/missing initial goal: keep uninitialized, reject intent/action;
    - valid new goal with invalid intent: accept only goal, independently check speech;
    - valid intent with invalid/unavailable action: reject that intent/action pair;
      goal may still initialize and valid speech may still commit;
    - null action with valid intent: accept a speech-only decision;
    - later rejected/missing action or invalid intent: use existing deterministic
      fallback, not old intent; goal and last accepted proposal remain unchanged;
    - aftermath: no goal/intent/action update, independent expression validation.
    Validate realization against eligible proposals independently; absence/invalid
    realization cannot invent an event. Invalid speech does not by itself reject
    an otherwise valid action/intent. Physical speech blocking prevents a speech-only
    intent from being recorded as a realized utterance; a decision is still only intent.
    Commit resulting state and actual speech at the existing atomic revision boundary.
    CAS conflict adopts none of that save. No acceptance success claims for failed saves.
    Initial-goal failure may be retried in the next ordinary prologue/turn slot only,
    not via an immediate new application call. No new expression/semantic repair;
    ADR0026 repair stays exclusively on old V2 psyche contracts.

decision D7 based_on D2, D3, D4, D5, D6, AUTHORITY:
  |
    V3 currentGoal, beliefs, interior appraisal and ExpressionBrief are legacy-only:
    initialize compatibility fields to their old neutral shape, do not give them
    new strategic writers, and never read them as V3 conscious meaning.
    Goal is consciousAgencyV1.upperGoal; current tactical appraisal/brief is Intent,
    not a copied old speechAppraisal or publicAim. Frozen unknown legacy beliefs
    are not migrated. Legacy V1/V2 keeps its existing writers and phase behavior.
    Executed reflect action may still append battleVolatileMemory through its
    existing engine writer; it must not overwrite V3 upperGoal or intent through
    currentGoal/interior side effects. Its observer-safe result enters next judgment
    as an executed result, not a new strategic state writer.
    Postbattle reflection reads the accepted V3 goal and committed action/speech
    evidence instead of stale currentGoal. No new character-memory write is added.
    Private memory and matchup memory remain in existing storage/lifecycle, but old
    psyche free text is not read into V3; new long-term memory selection is deferred.
    Canonical conversation history remains written by utterance commitment.
    Focus shadow remains no-effect, excluded from action authority.
    Seven tags: battle.ts psyche schema and llm/types psyche input remain legacy;
    deterministicPsyche dispatch gains explicit V3 no-call phase routing; stored
    matchup-memory projection is old-only; expressionState projection gets V3
    reaction/agency input; Compact psyche goal instructions become old-only; full
    psyche instructions remain old-only. Retained tags name their generation and
    reason. Do not delete all tags as proof of completed migration.

decision D8 based_on D2, D5, D6, AUTHORITY, E_CODE:
  |
    Reuse provider surfaces advanceCharacterAgent for V3 prologue/turn/aftermath
    and decideCharacterAction for eligible later redecision. Keep operation labels
    advanceCharacterAgentCompact and decideCharacterAction, taxonomy v2 layer
    characterExpression; labels are compatibility names, not distinct minds.
    Each eligible normal phase uses one logical conscious call per active side;
    later phase at most one logical redecision. Disabled/ineligible slots use zero.
    All V3 psyche phases use zero LLM calls. No critic/planner/application-repair call.
    Preserve existing transport retry policy: max2 retries total (rate-limit max2,
    service-unavailable max1 within that total), at most3 physical attempts per
    logical slot. Timeout or ineligible failure adds no new retry category.
    Provider admission/call/token/cost accounting includes every physical attempt.
    Do not reinterpret old runs; future replay binds exact contract and taxonomy,
    and reserves these worst-case attempts before paid approval.
    Public DTOs, narrator inputs and opponent inputs exclude agencyState, facts,
    private goal context and rationale except actual permitted expression.
    Internal default observability redacts the new state, existing private bindings and
    raw inputs/results; explicitly authorized raw access keeps its existing gate.

decision D9 based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D6, D7, D8, E_REVIEW, E_BASELINE:
  |
    Implement only after exact ADR acceptance in t029-A then B then C then D.
    A covers typed battle generation with existing character snapshots, state initialization/save/reload/CAS
    and opt-in validation; B pure reaction projection, conscious knowledge and closed
    adapter/mock; C later and partial failures; D legacy/privacy/accounting/7 tags.
    Add same personality/relationship with different authorship or confirmation
    and require identical allowed-goal sets. Add changed personality/relationship
    with fixed suggested objective and verify the appropriate goal/action sets change.
    Include explicit victory conflicting with enjoying combat or protecting a known
    counterpart; source status must not force victory. No unknown-origin start block.
    Add pure-projection no-tick and side-specific phase tests, unknown vs empty input,
    goal persistence over two judgments, current/historical ref separation, complete
    failure precedence, unavailable actions, repeated speech and observer privacy.
    Check V3 settings omitted/explicit version, mixed tuples, legacy override rejection,
    disabled slots, transport-attempt accounting and legacy/no-call regressions.
    Reuse F01-F08 allowed action sets and rubric; do not report fixed-response success
    as real-model improvement. t030 defines thresholds/ceilings; t031 approves paid
    execution. No publication, deployment, setting write or old-battle migration here.
    Costs are larger conscious inputs and battle-generation/acceptance code paths,
    not new character envelopes or author-confirmation UI. Benefits are connected
    character-grounded goal/action/speech judgment, not proven model improvement.
    Keep the 3p implementation estimate provisional until contract review; removing
    provenance work is not evidence that the remaining work takes exactly 3p.

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-09 owner stated: 新版で承認、実装を進めて。終了時間は２２：３０に延長
    Exact approved ADR0028 revision2 think SHA256 before this acceptance annotation:
    0629f788432b235bbc41f83e86e68d013d3850f58d04d80e313c97b4aa27b50a.
    Requirement v2 SHA256:
    5a30f561ff4ffdbbcc51ec41e4cc6e989191f51ab191f92f8f94c1c4c3bfda76.
    This is direct owner approval, not a claim of a second independent review.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    Accept exact ADR0028 revision2 D1-D9 and permit its local implementation.
    Preserve V1/V2, semantic goal fit and no author-origin gate.
    Paid execution, settings activation, deployment and publication remain separate.
